# publishing/substack-checklist.md

# Substack Publishing Checklist

Use this checklist before publishing every article in The Testimony After the Sermon.

---

## Required

- Article title follows the series format
- Opening Scripture is included
- Sermon number is included
- Sermon title is included
- Personal testimony voice is preserved
- The article is not written in Professor Enoch’s voice
- The sermon video link is included when available
- The article includes honest correction
- The article includes prayer
- The article connects to Surrender → Abide in Christ → Mirror → Water → Fire
- The article includes a Fifth Gospel reflection

---

## Voice Check

Before publishing, ask:

Does this sound like testimony or doctrine?

If it sounds like doctrine, move it to Medium.

If it sounds like lived witness, keep it on Substack.

---

## Closing Check

Every article should leave the reader with one truth:

The sermon was preached once.

Now the sermon must be lived daily.

---

# publishing/article-format-guide.md

# Article Format Guide

Each article in this series should follow the same structure.

---

# After Sermon [NUMBER]: [TITLE]

## What God Showed Me After I Preached

Opening Scripture:

"[SCRIPTURE]"

---

## What I Was Trying to Say

Explain the main burden of the sermon.

Do not over-polish this section.

Write it like testimony.

---

## What I Actually Lived While Preaching It

Describe the real moment.

This may include:

- The Rock
- The weather
- Your spirit
- Distractions
- Conviction
- Unexpected encounters
- What happened before or after the sermon

---

## What I Got Right

Name where the sermon aligned with Scripture, truth, and obedience.

---

## What I Should Have Corrected

Name what needed more clarity, humility, patience, scripture, or correction.

This is not shame.

This is formation.

---

## What I Prayed About Afterward

Write the actual prayer.

This section should feel like the altar after the sermon.

---

## What God Is Teaching Me Now

Connect the sermon to the formation flow:

Surrender → Abide in Christ → Mirror → Water → Fire

---

## The Fifth Gospel Reflection

Explain how your life must now become the message.

---

## Closing Witness

I preached the sermon once.

Now I have to live it daily.